2026-09-18T11:45:24.0579096Z       "body": "Follow-up to discussion #16355.\n\n## Problem\n\nRegistering the first route imports the whole `pydantic.v1` package, even in an app that only uses Pydantic v2:\n\n```\napp.py                         @app.get(\"/items\")\n  fastapi/routing.py             add_api_route -> get_dependant -> analyze_param\n    fastapi/utils.py               annotation_is_pydantic_v1(type_)\n      fastapi/_compat/shared.py      from pydantic import v1\n```\n\nSince #14609 dropped `pydantic.v1` support, both callers of this detection (`fastapi/utils.py` and `fastapi/encoders.py`) exist only to raise `PydanticV1NotSupportedError`. For a v2-only app the answer is always `False`, and the import is never used for anything else. The `encoders.py` call site can also hit it during request serialization for any object that falls through `ENCODERS_BY_TYPE`.\n\nCost measured on FastAPI 0.141.1 / Pydantic 2.13.5 / CPython 3.14:\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| AWS Lambda, arm64, 512 MB, cold start | **44 ms** median of 5 |\n| Local, warm bytecode, `fastapi` and `pydantic` already imported | 4.2 ms median of 5 |\n| On disk | 1.2 MB |\n\n## Change\n\nA `pydantic.v1` model class cannot exist unless `pydantic.v1` has already been imported, so `\"pydantic.v1\" in sys.modules` is a necessary condition for either detection function to ever return `True`. Both `is_pydantic_v1_model_class` and `is_pydantic_v1_model_instance` now return `False` early when that key is absent, before touching the import.\n\nBehavior is unchanged for anyone who does define a v1 model: they imported `pydantic.v1` to do so, so they still get `PydanticV1NotSupportedError` with the same message. The only way to bypass the check is deleting `sys.modules[\"pydantic.v1\"]` after defining a model, which is not a supported pattern.\n\n## Tests\n\nTwo tests added to `tests/test_compat.py`, both using `monkeypatch.delitem(sys.modules, \"pydantic.v1\", raising=False)` so they are independent of test order:\n\n- unit: both detection functions return `False` for a v2 model and `pydantic.v1` stays out of `sys.modules`\n- integration: an app with a v2 body model handles a request end to end without importing `pydantic.v1`\n\nThe existing `tests/test_pydantic_v1_error.py` still passes, covering the branch after the guard.\n",
